            "The result is a negative one on a task agents are widely marketed for: wrapping a retriever in an agent loop made the retrieval worse, not better, on labels supplied by the papers' own authors.",
            "The paper is a preprint and has not been peer reviewed. The labels capture what authors say did or could have inspired their work, which is a judgement made after the fact, and the paper notes one model may have seen the finished papers in training."
          ],
          "topics": ["evals", "agents", "ai-for-science"],
          "impact": "neutral",
          "flags": ["preprint"]
